meta {
  name: Download Quote Recap Document
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/deal-audits/deals/{{auditDealId}}/quote-recap/document/download
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{auditReviewerToken}}
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200, or 404 when the sale's quote has no document", function () {
    // The demo seed writes nothing to object storage, so its recaps carry no
    // document and this is a 404 there. Either way the route answered, which
    // proves the manager reaches it without `quote_recaps:read`.
    expect([200, 404]).to.include(res.getStatus());
  });

  test("a document comes back as a short-lived inline link", function () {
    if (res.getStatus() === 200) {
      const body = res.getBody();
      expect(body.downloadUrl).to.be.a("string");
      expect(body.filename).to.be.a("string");
      expect(body.contentType).to.be.a("string");
      expect(body.expiresIn).to.be.a("number");
    }
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /deal-audits/deals/:dealId/quote-recap/document/download — the quote PDF (PAC-106)

  "View quote document" in the Deal Audit page's quote recap drawer.

  - **Module:** `deal_audits`
  - **Permission:** `deal_audits:read` **and** `management:read`.
  - **Data scope:** the deal's audit must be in the caller's reach.

  ⚠ Its own route rather than `GET /quote-recaps/:id/document/download`: that
  one is gated on `quote_recaps:read`, which the Branch Manager template does
  not hold. Reaching the document **through the audit** is the access the
  manager has.

  The recap is the one the deal names (`quoteRecapId`), else the lead's most
  recent recap on or before the sold day — the same rule **Get Deal Audit
  Review** shows as `quoteRecap`.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "downloadUrl": "https://…/agencies/…/quote.pdf?X-Amz-…",
    "filename": "quote.pdf",
    "contentType": "application/pdf",
    "expiresIn": 300
  }
  ```

  Presigned **inline** (`Content-Disposition: inline`), so it opens in a tab
  rather than downloading. A presigned URL is a bearer capability: minted per
  read, never stored.

  ## Errors
  - `403 Forbidden` — missing `deal_audits:read` or `management:read`.
  - `404 Not Found` — no audit for that deal, out of reach, no quote recap, or
    a recap with no uploaded document.
}
